# Swaytastic: desktop / file-manager icons not showing

Swaytastic is SVG-only. install.sh uses `apt --no-install-recommends`, so the
SVG *libraries* were installed but not the *plugins* that actually paint icons.

- pcmanfm-qt (desktop + file manager): needs Qt SVG icon engine
  had libqt6svg6 (.so only), missing qt6-svg-plugins (libqsvgicon.so)
- Thunar (GTK): needs gdk-pixbuf SVG loader
  had librsvg2-2 (.so only), missing librsvg2-common (libpixbufloader_svg.so)

Without those plugins Qt draws empty icons, and GTK cannot use Swaytastic SVGs
so Thunar falls back to Adwaita PNGs.

Also: theme inherited only hicolor (almost empty), so anything Swaytastic does
not ship had no real icon. QSS styled QListView::item globally, which can stop
Qt drawing decorations on the desktop list view.

After applying: re-run host/guest install.sh (or apt install the two packages),
`sudo gtk-update-icon-cache -f /usr/share/icons/Swaytastic`, restart pcmanfm-qt
and reopen Thunar.

---

## 1. host/install.sh  and  guest/install.sh

In PACKAGES, immediately after `libqt6svg6`, add:

  qt6-svg-plugins
  librsvg2-common

## 2. local/icons/Swaytastic/index.theme

- Inherits=hicolor
+ Inherits=Adwaita,hicolor

On the Directories= line, drop `symbolic/emblems` (that directory is not in the
shipped theme).

Delete the whole unused block:

  [symbolic/emblems]
  Size=16
  MinSize=1
  MaxSize=512
  Context=Emblems
  Type=Scalable

## 3. local/icons/recolor-adwaita.py

In the INDEX string:

- Inherits=hicolor
+ Inherits=Adwaita,hicolor

(Leave emblems in this generator INDEX; a full Adwaita copy may include that dir.)

## 4. local/qss/Swaytastic.qss

Scope item rules to folder windows so they do not apply to the desktop
layer-shell QListView. Same pattern already used for QListView fill.

Replace the two global item rules with:

QMainWindow QTreeView::item, QDialog QTreeView::item,
QMainWindow QListView::item, QDialog QListView::item,
QMainWindow QTableView::item, QDialog QTableView::item {
    padding: 5px 8px;
    min-height: 22px;
}

QMainWindow QTreeView::item:selected, QDialog QTreeView::item:selected,
QMainWindow QListView::item:selected, QDialog QListView::item:selected,
QMainWindow QTableView::item:selected, QDialog QTableView::item:selected {
    background: #de1062;
    color: #99e01c;
}

XDG_DESKTOP_DIR="$HOME" is intentional and was not the bug. No change there.
